blocks.en:
We compare five training variants:
raw rubric reward;
OP, which uses only the preference reward r pref r_{\mathrm{pref}} ;
MR, which sums the aggregate rubric and preference rewards;
FRDA+OP, which adds the preference reward as another dimension
in FRDA without whitening;
and RSDC, which applies Cholesky whitening to the joint
advantage vector before aggregation, with the preference
dimension placed last.
All variants use Qwen3-4B ( Qwen Team, 2025 ) as policy model and are evaluated on Arena-Hard v2.0 ( Li et al., 2024 ) .

